  "chapter": {
    "number": 98,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(99) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord reigns; —let the people rage; it is he that sits upon the cherubs, let the earth be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is great in Sion, and is high over all the people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them give thanks to your great name; for it is terrible and holy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And the king's honor loves judgment; you have prepared",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 190
          },
          {
            "text": "equity, you have wrought judgment and justice in Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Exalt you⌃ the Lord our God, and worship at his footstool; for he is holy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Moses and Aaron among his priests, and Samuel among them that call upon his name; they called upon the Lord, and he heard them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He spoke to them in a pillar of cloud; they kept his testimonies, and the ordinances which he gave them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord our God, you heard them; O God, you became propitious to them, though you did take vengeance on all their devices.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Exalt you⌃ the Lord our God, and worship at his holy mountain; for the Lord our God is holy.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 190,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. equities.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 98,
          "verse": 4
        }
      }
    ]
